# GitHub API needs full_network

Cursor's default Shell sandbox **blocks** `https://api.github.com` (HTTP 403 / connection failure). This bot is entirely API-driven — never run discovery, follow, or raw `curl`/`requests` against GitHub without elevated network.

## Required

When the Shell tool talks to GitHub (directly or via the bot), pass:

```text
required_permissions: ["full_network"]
```

Use `["all"]` only if sandbox FS/syscalls also block the command (rare here).

## Apply on first try (do not stumble)

Request `full_network` **up front** for:

- `./run.sh`, `python -m bot`, any discovery/follow run
- `curl` / `gh` / `pip` hitting the public internet or GitHub
- Scripts that call `api.github.com` (search, filters, follow)

Do **not**:

1. Run the bot or API call in the default sandbox
2. Diagnose a 403 / timeout as an app bug
3. Narrate “сеть заблокирована — перезапускаю…” after a failed attempt

## Symptom → fix

| Symptom | Cause | Action |
|---------|--------|--------|
| `403 Forbidden` from `api.github.com` in Shell | Sandbox allowlist | Re-run with `full_network` |
| Tool note: “Network access: Limited” | Same | Same |
| Auth `401` / rate-limit `403` with `X-RateLimit-*` | Real API response | Fix token / wait — not a sandbox issue |

## Examples

```bash
# ✅ GOOD — Shell tool with required_permissions: ["full_network"]
cd /home/starl/GitHubFollowerBot && ./run.sh
curl -sI https://api.github.com

# ❌ BAD — default sandbox; api.github.com returns 403
curl -sI https://api.github.com
python -m bot
```
